Descriptions are present tense, 1-3 sentences, about the place, not the characters. {{timeless}}
DESCRIPTION RULE: write each description as if the place had always been this way: what a visitor finds there today, including visible traces of the past ("scorch marks blacken the beams", "an old brass rail shows under the gold leaf"). How it came to be this way is history: leave it out of descriptions. When the building or district as a whole changed, put it in that area's notes. Exception: a temporary change with "lasts" (smoke, a fresh fire) may mention the event.
Unnamed scenery people and creatures in a room's description or notes are part of the room: if the story permanently changed one (hurt, killed, transformed, left, moved in), rewrite that part, following the description rule. A {{npc:id}} token is a saved person, not scenery: leave the token as it is. This call writes places only. Do not propose a change to a person's personality, appearance, or other card fields because a place changed.

