Which places did the story change on the map, for good or for a while? Put an area id in areas only when the building or district as a whole changed: it was renamed, or its notes no longer hold. One room changing is a room, not its area. Reply {"rooms": [addresses that changed], "areas": []}, or {"rooms": [], "areas": []} if nothing on the map changed.

You turn a real change to places in a story, permanent or temporary, into a map patch. {{reply}}: {"ops": [...]}.
ADDR is a room's full address copied exactly from the map, e.g. "riverton:drowned_rat/common_room". AREA is a region id ("riverton") or subregion id ("riverton:drowned_rat"). Never invent addresses or ids: renaming a place changes its display name only, its address stays the same.
Allowed ops (exactly what the map editor can do):
{{edit_types}}
Example, light touch, one room (a smashed bar): {"ops":[{"op":"set_description","loc":"riverton:drowned_rat/common_room","text":"<the same description with only the bar sentence changed>"}]}
Example, a full rewrite (a whole inn turned into a palace): {"ops":[{"op":"update_area","area":"riverton:drowned_rat","name":"The Golden Palace","lore":"<the area's whole notes, rewritten for the palace, keeping what still holds; then: formerly the Drowned Rat inn, turned into a palace by magic>"},{"op":"set_description","loc":"riverton:drowned_rat/common_room","text":"A gilded throne hall; an old brass rail shows under the gold leaf."},{"op":"set_description","loc":"riverton:drowned_rat/courtyard","text":"..."}]}
update_area and append_lore are for a building that changed as a whole.
A temporary but real change (a portal open for 1 hour, a room filled with smoke, a tunnel blocked for a day) counts: give its ops "lasts" with how long it holds, e.g. "1h", "12h", "3d". Any op may add "lasts". Use as few ops as possible. {{style}}
Exit names (the "direction", e.g. "grate", "narrow door") are hand-written: never rename them. A door's open/locked/blocked state and removing an exit apply to both sides; hidden, sight and text are per side. Only change what the story clearly changed. Moment-to-moment action that leaves no trace on a place is not a change. If nothing on the map changed, reply {"ops": []}.
If the story changed the map in a way none of these ops can express, do not force a wrong op: reply {"cant": "one short sentence saying what can't be shown on the map"}.

